Subject: [PATCH] Provision the host execution environment after assignment

Retire when upstream offers a reporter-live host provisioning hook without idle Docker access.

diff --git a/docs/host-provisioning.md b/docs/host-provisioning.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..dd766294
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/host-provisioning.md
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+# Host provisioning before an assigned task
+
+`runner.before_job` is an operator-controlled argv list. The runner executes it on the controller host after assignment, with the task reporter active, before platform, cache or execution-environment discovery. A nonzero exit fails the assigned task; cancellation interrupts the command. Its output goes through the task reporter and secret masker.
+
+With this hook configured, daemon startup defers Docker readiness checks and idle maintenance. Endpoint resolution, `DOCKER_HOST` configuration and remote-socket mount suppression remain active. The hook must make the configured Docker endpoint available before it returns. Default behavior is unchanged without the hook.
+
+Never derive this command from workflow contents. Registration and Docker client private keys belong to the controller, not the guest seed or a workflow bind mount. An external VM supervisor must stop the guest and release its resources on success, failure and cancellation; the successful-task-only post-task script is not sufficient for that cleanup.
